1. Scope and acceptance
"Software" means the project-owned code and documentation distributed with
this license. "Modified Software" includes changes to, and works incorporating
or derived from, the Software. Independent programs that only communicate
with the Software over MCP are not Modified Software under this license.
Third-party dependencies and FontLab itself are not licensed under these terms.
Exercising the permissions below constitutes acceptance of their conditions.

2. Free use and outputs
You may use the Software without charge, including in professional and
commercial font-design, engineering, research and consulting work. You may
use it with proprietary FontLab installations and independent MCP clients.
Fonts, outlines, feature files, reports and other user-created outputs are not
subject to this license merely because the Software processed or produced them.
You retain your rights in your inputs and outputs and may keep or sell them.

3. Copying, modification and source availability
You may inspect, copy, modify and redistribute the Software without charging
for it, subject to this license. Every redistribution of Software or Modified
Software must include this license, copyright notices, a clear account of
changes, and its complete corresponding source in the preferred form for
modification, including build/install scripts. Credentials, personal data, font inputs and
user-created outputs are excluded; provide documented configuration templates
instead of secrets. That source must also be
available to the public, without payment, under this same license. You may
not impose additional restrictions on recipients' exercise of these rights.

You may not incorporate the Software into a closed-source or proprietary
derivative, library, application or service. When deploying Modified Software
for operational use, including internal production use or a network service,
you must publicly provide its complete corresponding source under this
license. Private experiments and tests may remain private until operational
deployment or redistribution. These obligations apply to the Software and
its derivatives, not independent clients, FontLab, or user-created fonts.

4. Contributing deployed modifications upstream
For each version of Modified Software, within 30 days after its first
redistribution or operational deployment, submit all modifications in that
version not already submitted to the original project's public contribution channel as
a pull request, or as a source patch linked from an issue if pull requests
are unavailable. Your submission must identify the changes and provide the
complete source required by section 3. If the original project no longer has
a working public contribution channel, publish the changes in a publicly
accessible repository and identify the original project and this license.
You need not obtain acceptance or wait for a review, and maintainers are not
required to accept your submission. Merely using an unmodified copy does not
require a contribution.

5. No sale or paid software offering
You may not sell, rent, sublicense for payment, or otherwise charge for access
to the Software or Modified Software. You may not bundle it into a paid
software product or offer a paid hosted service whose material functionality
is the Software. This does not prohibit charging for independently created
fonts, font engineering, training or support, provided payment is not a
condition of obtaining or using the Software itself and no prohibited paid
software offering is made.

6. Contributions and third-party rights
Contributors retain copyright in their contributions and submit them under
this same license. No copyright assignment is required. You must have the
rights to submit your contribution. No rights to FontLab trademarks, code,
